---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.5 · Quest Cleanup, Dragon Slayer II & Desert Treasure II" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-5" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.5</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Quest Cleanup, Dragon Slayer II &amp; Desert Treasure II</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Close the remaining Quest Cape loose ends, take the last Runecraft level only when it is needed, and finish both old Grandmasters with the gear this route actually owns.</p>
      </header>
      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Quest Cape cleanup and DT2 prerequisite chains → Dragon Slayer II → live Runecraft remainder to 60 → Desert Treasure II → carry the live skill tab into the final chapter."
        stats={["Actual 60 Runecraft is the only new universal skill gate", "75+ Magic and Ranged, 74+ Slayer, Fire Cape and 70+ Crafting carry in", "Dragon Slayer II gives 80,000 Smithing XP before the later Blood Moon Rises check"]}
        unlocks={["Contact!, Beneath Cursed Sands, Secrets of the North and the DT2 miniquests", "Myths' Guild, Ring of shadows and Scar essence access", "No Bowfa, blowpipe, RCB drop, Slayer helmet, trident or Ava's assembler requirement"]}
      />
      <div class="callout"><strong>Quest journal first.</strong> This page closes quests the mandatory route had not actually checked off, not every optional activity a returning player may have sampled. A Ruff Situation and Crab Quest were completed in 3.3. Learning the Ropes is Tutorial Island, already completed before Chapter 1. If your journal already shows any cleanup quest green, skip its work; still check that every named quest is green before attempting a Quest Cape.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Quest Cape cleanup · currently released quests</div><h2>Close the old loose ends before the Grandmasters.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-prince-ali" number="1" title="Complete Prince Ali Rescue">
        <p>This easy classic was never scheduled earlier. Start with <strong>Hassan in Al Kharid Palace</strong>, then work with Osman and Leela around Al Kharid/Draynor to disguise the prince and get him past the jail guard. Bring a little cash, a few free inventory spaces and convenient Al Kharid/Draynor teleports; buy or make the quest's rope, dye/disguise and skin-paste materials as prompted. The reason to do it <em>now</em> is concrete: <strong>Contact! requires it</strong>. Do not retrofit it into Chapter 1. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Prince_Ali_Rescue" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest reference</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-classic-cleanup" number="2" title="Clear the remaining classic Quest Cape entries">
        <p>Check the journal, then finish <strong>The Corsair Curse, Scorpion Catcher, Spirits of the Elid, Ratcatchers, Rag and Bone Man I, Rag and Bone Man II, Olaf's Quest and Grim Tales</strong> if they are still red. They were absent or explicitly deferred in the mandatory route; none requires redesigning Chapters 1–2. Quest Helper may handle dialogue, but do the long item/bone collection in sensible trips rather than carrying every quest's kit at once.</p>
        <p><strong>Practical preparation:</strong> Corsair Curse is a short Corsair Cove investigation; Scorpion Catcher uses the already-completed Alfred Grimhand barcrawl, a scorpion cage and Taverley/Seers travel; Spirits of the Elid starts in Nardah and needs desert travel and a rope. Bring a <strong>cat</strong>, fish/food for it and poison protection for Ratcatchers' stealth and rat areas. Rag and Bone Man I leads into II: keep the requested special bones, then prepare the required vinegar pots/boiling step for II. Olaf's Quest takes cold-weather travel, a spade and combat supplies. For Grim Tales, the route already clears its Woodcutting/Herblore/Farming/Agility/Thieving checks; bring an axe, two tarromin potions (unf), watering can, seed dibber and food for Glod. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Quests/List" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest list</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-varlamore-cleanup" number="3" title="Finish the currently released Varlamore and Lumbridge loose ends">
        <p>Complete <strong>The Ides of Milk</strong> (start with Cassius by Lumbridge pond), then <strong>The Ribbiting Tale of a Lily Pad Labour Dispute</strong> (Marcellus at Locus Oasis; bring an axe), <strong>Meat and Greet</strong> (Emelio in Outer Fortis), <strong>At First Light</strong> (Guildmaster Apatura at the Hunter Guild; Eagles' Peak is already done; bring a needle, hammer and a box trap or two jerboa tails), and <strong>Shadows of Custodia</strong> (read the Auburn Pub notice board; bring four willow longbows, four maple logs, a fishing rod and combat food). The route already exceeds the latter quests' skill checks. These are Quest Cape completions, not requirements for Jad or a new gear farm. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Quests/List" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest list</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-contact" number="4" title="Complete Contact! immediately after Prince Ali Rescue">
        <p><strong>Icthlarin's Little Helper and Gertrude's Cat</strong> are already complete. Speak to the High Priest in Sophanem. Bring a reliable, preferably non-extinguishable light source, a tinderbox backup, antipoison, food, Prayer restores and an exit teleport. The Scabarite dungeon is the awkward part: traps can extinguish ordinary lights, so do not enter with only an unrelightable option. For the level-191 Giant Scarab, use the route's ranged/magic kit, maintain the relevant protection prayer and keep enough food to survive mistakes. Claim <strong>7,000 Thieving XP, Keris and Sophanem bank/shop access</strong>.</p>
        <p>The combat reward is <strong>one bankable lamp with two separate 7,000-XP choices</strong> from Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged or Magic—not two lamps and not a Slayer option. With actual 75 Magic already solved, put both choices into <strong>Strength by default</strong> unless the live account has a better immediate combat need. Record two allocations from the one reward, exactly once. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Contact!" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Contact! mechanics</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-beneath-sands" number="5" title="Complete Beneath Cursed Sands">
        <p>Do this after Contact!. Its actual <strong>62 Agility, 55 Crafting and 55 Firemaking</strong> checks are already cleared. Start with <strong>Jamila at her Sophanem stall</strong>, then meet Maisa; bank-check a <strong>coal, iron bar, tinderbox, spade and valid meat</strong> before the multi-area trip. Bring desert heat protection, food, restores, antipoison and the normal melee/ranged switches. The Head Menaphite Guard punishes active protection prayers, so bring real food and turn overheads off for that fight. Kite the Champion of Scabaras with Ranged and <strong>Protect from Magic</strong>, and re-bank for the later Menaphite Akh/scarab-mage fights as needed. Claim <strong>50,000 Agility XP</strong> and the <strong>Keris partisan</strong>. Tombs of Amascut access is a useful unlock, but completing the raid is optional post-guide content. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Beneath_Cursed_Sands" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest reference</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Mahjarrat chain · mandatory miniquests only</div><h2>Connect the actual DT2 prerequisites.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-enakhra" number="6" title="Complete Enakhra's Lament on the standard spellbook">
        <p>Start with Lazim just north-east of the Desert Quarry. The checks are <strong>50 Crafting and 43 Prayer, not boostable; 39 Magic and the listed 45 Firemaking check are boostable</strong> (the Firemaking level helps identify brazier fuel rather than preventing trial-and-error). The route exceeds them. Make a one-trip kit: <strong>chisel, tinderbox, ordinary candle, normal/oak/willow/maple logs, a whole acceptable food item for Pentyn, soft clay, coal and pickaxe</strong>; bring a water container if making the clay onsite. Mine <strong>52 kg of sandstone and two 5 kg granite pieces</strong> at the quarry if not banked. Use standard-book runes for a wind bolt/blast/wave or better, a fire bolt/blast/wave or better, and <strong>Crumble Undead</strong> (bring spare casts); keep enough Prayer for a short Protect from Melee use. Desert heat supplies and a teleport make the trip less brittle. Claim the fixed <strong>7,000 XP each in Crafting, Mining, Firemaking and Magic</strong>, then read live levels without projecting extra gates. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Enakhra%27s_Lament/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">One-trip item reference</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-empty-lord" number="7" title="Complete Curse of the Empty Lord and claim its museum lamp">
        <p>Use the <strong>ring of visibility</strong> from Desert Treasure I and a <strong>ghostspeak amulet</strong> to follow the current ghost sequence for all six pieces of <strong>Ghostly robes</strong>. Some stops are in the Wilderness. Bank valuables, take only replaceable travel/combat kit where needed, enable <strong>PK skull prevention</strong>, check your world and teleport limits, and never assume a quiet Wilderness is safe. On completion, show the full set to Historian Minas in the Varrock Museum for the <strong>10,000-XP antique lamp</strong> (skill level 50+). Put it in <strong>Fletching by default</strong> toward the later actual-70 Blood Moon Rises gate; do not silently treat it as having already reached that level. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Curse_of_the_Empty_Lord" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ghost route</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-general-shadow" number="8" title="Complete The General's Shadow">
        <p>Full Ghostly robes, <strong>Fight Arena</strong> and the ring of visibility now cover the chain. Speak to the ghost of General Khazard south-east of Rellekka with the <strong>ghostspeak amulet, ring, all six robe pieces and at least 40 coins</strong>; use ordinary teleports for the scattered scouts. Bring ranged/magic combat kit and food for the level-160 <strong>Ghost of Bouncer</strong> in the Goblin Cave. <strong>Prayer cannot be used in that cave fight</strong>; safespot rather than relying on an overhead. Claim its fixed <strong>2,000 Slayer XP</strong> as incidental—the actual-74 Slayer gate was already closed in 3.4. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_General%27s_Shadow/Quick_guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Scout and fight reference</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-secrets" number="9" title="Complete Secrets of the North; do not farm Phantom Muspah">
        <p>The hard <strong>69 Agility, 64 Thieving and 56 Hunter</strong> gates are already behind us. Check the journal for <strong>Making Friends with My Arm, The General's Shadow, Devious Minds and Hazeel Cult</strong>; only the General's Shadow branch was newly closed here. Start with the guard outside the Carnillean Mansion in East Ardougne. Bring <strong>100 coins and a normal lockpick</strong> (the Strange Old Lockpick does not work), plus a tinderbox, antipoison, food, Prayer restores and Weiss transport. Evelot, the Assassin and the Strange Creature are separate supply/combat phases: bank between them, move away from Assassin poison projectiles, and use the deterministic ranged/magic gear for the Strange Creature while learning its attack cycle. Claim <strong>60,000 Agility, 50,000 Thieving and 40,000 Hunter XP</strong>. The post-quest Phantom Muspah and its drops are optional. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Secrets_of_the_North" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest reference</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-faithful" number="10" title="Complete His Faithful Servants, not a Barrows gear grind">
        <p>With Priest in Peril done, speak to the <strong>Strange Old Man at Barrows</strong> east of Mort'ton. Bring a <strong>spade</strong>, Barrows travel, Magic/combat gear, food and Prayer restores. Dig each of the six mounds and defeat its brother; one randomized mound leads to the tunnel instead, where the final brother appears on the way to the chest. Open that chest with <strong>at least six free inventory spaces</strong> so the strange icon is actually received; if a full inventory prevents the pickup, you may need to repeat the brothers. Then return it to the Old Man. No Barrows unique is needed. Claim the <strong>20,000 Prayer-XP lamp</strong>. This miniquest is mandatory specifically for DT2; other optional miniquests are not being pulled into the route. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/His_Faithful_Servants" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Miniquest reference</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Dragon Slayer II · before the final RC bridge</div><h2>Audit the bank, then take the first Grandmaster.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-ds2-preflight" number="11" title="Secure the Dragon Slayer II quest kit and live boss supplies">
        <p>Check <strong>200 quest points, actual 75 Magic, 70 Smithing, 68 Mining, 62 Crafting, 60 Agility, 60 Thieving, 50 Construction and 50 Hitpoints</strong> in the journal/skill tab. This route should clear them, but check live Hitpoints instead of inferring it from other combat levels. The direct prior quests are <strong>Legends' Quest, Dream Mentor, A Tail of Two Cats, Animal Magnetism, Ghosts Ahoy, Bone Voyage and Client of Kourend</strong>; check their own prerequisite chains in the journal rather than relying on a remembered quest-point total. Start with Alec Kincade outside the Myths' Guild after every required prior quest is green. Reserve a real food/restore/teleport/cash buffer; Chapter 3 has no guaranteed ending coin stack.</p>
        <p><strong>Ancient Cavern access is a separate mandatory partial miniquest check.</strong> The Chapter 1 Barbarian Fishing foundation alone does not prove it. At Otto's Grotto, finish the first Barbarian Firemaking demonstration (light the taught fire with a bow), then ask Otto specifically about <strong>pyre ships</strong> so the whirlpool admits you to the Ancient Cavern for DS2's key-forging phase. You do <em>not</em> need to farm chewed bones or finish every Barbarian Training section. Bring a one-click teleport when first entering the dangerous cavern. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ancient_Cavern" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Access condition</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Bank audit:</strong> adamant crossbow (or already-owned RCB), <em>remaining</em> plain adamant, ruby (e) and diamond (e) bolts from 3.3, Ava's accumulator, anti-dragon shield, antifire doses, poison/venom cures, food, Prayer restores and optional run/restoration supplies. For quest phases check <strong>insulated boots, axe, machete, hammer, saw, 8 oak planks, 10 swamp paste and spare nails; catspeak and ghostspeak access; retained goutweed; cut dragonstone, 2 molten glass, glassblowing pipe and spade; 1 astral rune; seal of passage for Lunar Isle if still applicable; tinderbox, pestle and mortar; and runes for three Fire Wave or Fire Surge casts</strong>. Bank/regear by phase; this is a whole-quest checklist, not one inventory.</p>
        <p><strong>Dragonstone fallback:</strong> search for a cut/uncut dragonstone, complete crystal key or both key halves <em>before</em> farming anything. If a key/halves exist, combine the halves if needed, open the <strong>Taverley crystal chest for its guaranteed uncut dragonstone</strong>, then cut it with the route's 70+ Crafting. If none exists, fight <strong>Goraks on the Gorak Plane via fairy ring DIR</strong> for both key halves: the main gem table lists approximately <strong>1/128 for the loop half and 1/128 for the tooth half</strong>. Bring strong defensive/crush-resistant gear, food, restore/stat-recovery supplies as needed, and fairy-ring/teleport access. Protection prayers do <em>not</em> block Gorak attacks. A ring of wealth improves the rates <em>if already owned</em>; making one now would be circular because it consumes a dragonstone. Combine the halves, open the Taverley chest for its <strong>guaranteed</strong> uncut dragonstone, cut it, and continue DS2. This is a repeatable RNG bridge for a mandatory material, <strong>not a fixed kill count or a dragonstone drop from Goraks</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Gorak" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Gorak drops and combat</a> · <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Crystal_chest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Guaranteed chest reward</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-ds2" number="12" title="Complete Dragon Slayer II with the retained ranged kit">
        <p>Use the <strong>adamant crossbow</strong> (RCB only if already owned), anti-dragon shield, Ava's accumulator and banked d'hide/Barrows gloves. For the quest <strong>Vorkath</strong>, pre-pot before entry—it wakes immediately in the quest—and use shield <em>plus</em> ordinary antifire for two dragonfire layers. Protect from Missiles for a ranged crossbow setup, cure poison/venom, move at once from the lobbed fireball, keep walking during acid and use <strong>Crumble Undead</strong> on the spawn (or a ranged hit if prepared). Ruby (e) is for high HP; switch to diamond (e) as HP falls. Keep enough supplies for retries, not an invented fixed bolt consumption.</p>
        <p>The fleet has checkpoints between sections; <strong>Galvek's own four-phase fight has none</strong>. Refill after a checkpoint. On Galvek, shield + antifire remain the ordinary baseline; Protect from Magic in phase 1, then Protect from Missiles for later ranged phases. Move <strong>two tiles away</strong> from the launched fireball; antifire does not stop that special. Avoid phase-1 fire traps, phase-3 tsunami through its gap, and the phase-4 binding rock; keep run energy and Auto Retaliate off. Ruby (e) helps against his large HP pool, then diamond (e) near the end (around 150 HP). Do not require Bowfa, blowpipe, dragon crossbow, crystal armour or Rigour. The lower-tier kit may take practice and multiple trips.</p>
        <p><strong>Death/retry:</strong> the DS2 dream, Vorkath and fleet/Galvek instances use deathbanks, not free Fight-Cave-style retries. Torfinn can reclaim the Vorkath/fleet items for <strong>100,000 coins</strong>; retrieve a deathbank promptly before any further unsafe death, which can erase its contents. Check Hardcore status separately. The first failure should teach a mechanic or supply adjustment, not trigger a rare-weapon hunt. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dragon_Slayer_II" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current fight, checkpoint and reclaim guide</a>.</p>
        <p>Claim the fixed <strong>80,000 Smithing, 60,000 Mining, 50,000 Agility and 50,000 Thieving XP</strong>. Speak to <strong>Ellen in the Myths' Guild</strong> for <strong>four separate 25,000-XP combat selections</strong>, each eligible for Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged or Magic. They are post-quest dialogue rewards, not automatically spent at the quest-complete screen; claim and record all four now so deferral cannot be forgotten. With actual 75 Magic already solved, choose <strong>Strength by default</strong> unless a live combat need is clearer. Count the four rewards once. The Smithing XP reduces the later Blood Moon Rises actual-72 remainder; do not claim it completes that gate without checking live XP.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <ExpandableNote title="Recommended later upgrade: Ava's assembler" label="Optional; never Quest Cape progress">
        <p>Post-quest Vorkath can drop a head early, and the head is guaranteed by kill 50 if still dry. Bring it to Ava with the required materials to upgrade the accumulator if you <em>want</em> that permanent ranged improvement. Up to 50 extra boss kills are not part of graduation, and neither the head nor assembler is required for DT2. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Vorkath%27s_head" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Head guarantee</a>.</p>
      </ExpandableNote>

      <section><div class="section-label">Only remaining DT2 skill gate</div><h2>Train the live Runecraft remainder, no farther.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-rc-60" number="13" title="Reach actual 60 Runecraft for Desert Treasure II">
        <p>The conservative Fremennik Exiles exit was <strong>196,636 Runecraft XP</strong>; actual 60 begins at <strong>273,742 XP</strong>. Thus the <em>maximum</em> untouched remainder is <strong>273,742 − 196,636 = 77,106 XP</strong>. Read the live XP now and train only <strong>max(0, 273,742 − live RC XP)</strong>. Use existing essence/pouches first. <strong>Guardians of the Rift</strong>, explained in 3.2, is the default structured loop; <strong>Ourania/ZMI</strong> is a reasonable change of pace. Stop at actual 60. No 65-RC diary grind or fixed essence mountain belongs here. <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-2/`}>3.2 Runecraft primer</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Desert Treasure II · the Fallen Empire</div><h2>Four distinct boss lanes, then the final sequence.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i35-dt2-preflight" number="14" title="Verify every Desert Treasure II gate and prepare modular supplies">
        <p>Check actual <strong>75 Firemaking, 75 Magic, 70 Thieving, 62 Herblore, 60 Runecraft and 60 Construction</strong>. In the journal, verify <strong>Desert Treasure I, Secrets of the North, Enakhra's Lament, Temple of the Eye, The Garden of Death, Below Ice Mountain and His Faithful Servants</strong> are green; the long Making Friends with My Arm/General's Shadow/Devious Minds/Hazeel Cult chain is already consumed by Secrets. Start at the <strong>Ancient Vault north-east of Nardah</strong> only when those checks pass.</p>
        <p>Bring the ring of visibility, <strong>Ancient Magicks</strong> and enough runes for <strong>Blood, Ice, Smoke and Shadow Burst</strong> to open the initial route (at least 8 death, 16 chaos, 2 fire, 3 air, 4 water, 2 soul and 2 blood runes). <strong>Use Ancients whenever stunning the Leviathan with Shadow spells; switch to the standard spellbook before any Whisperer attempt using the Earth Wave baseline below.</strong> Keep a <strong>facemask from a Slayer equipment shop</strong> for the choking passages in The Scar; a Slayer helmet is not assumed. A pickaxe, tinderbox and pestle can be obtained in the quest, but carrying familiar tools may be simpler. For each boss attempt, take its one primary weapon set and small mechanic switch, a one-click exit where usable, a few Prayer restores, any relevant antipoison/energy and then fill the remaining slots with real food. Travel supplies and a modest banked rune reserve matter more than speculative upgrades. Bank and rebuild inventory between the four lanes; do not try to carry four bosses' kits at once. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Desert_Treasure_II_-_The_Fallen_Empire" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current prerequisites and quest phases</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i35-dt2" number="15" title="Complete Desert Treasure II with deterministic melee, ranged and Magic setups">
        <p><strong>Baseline:</strong> dragon scimitar or the route's situational Arkan blade, dragon defender, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, Piety and normal defensive gear for melee; adamant crossbow/optional owned RCB, Ava's accumulator, banked d'hide and <em>remaining</em> plain/diamond (e) bolts for range. Use ruby (e) only where a high-HP target makes it worthwhile; the 3.3 quantities were an initial shared buffer, not a fresh refill at every boss. For Magic, the <strong>one-time 80,000-coin Ancient staff from Eblis after DT1</strong> can autocast both Ancient and standard combat spells, provided you are on the matching spellbook. It is a purchasable weapon floor, not a trident drop. Bank-check affordable runes and a magic-accuracy outfit before each attempt. No powered staff, Slayer drop or rare magic armour is universal.</p>
        <p><strong>Vardorvis — melee/slash:</strong> use dragon scimitar/defender, Protect from Melee and Piety. His auto-attacks heal him, so keep prayer up; shift around the arena's edge to miss axes and floor spikes, briefly switch to Protect from Missiles for the head projectile that disables overheads, and click away the red spores. The fight accelerates as HP drops. Re-bank before the Kasonde follow-up. <strong>Leviathan — range:</strong> stay outside bite range with the crossbow and read orb colours on impact: blue Magic, green Missiles, orange Melee. Cast a <strong>Shadow spell</strong> with the Ancient staff to stun, then attack from behind to reset the accelerating attack rhythm; run around lightning, move off falling-rock shadows and use a boulder for the smoke blast. At the final 20%, follow the moving abyssal pathfinder so prayers work and attacks gain accuracy. The Shadow cast is a mechanic, not a mandate to train Magic beyond 75.</p>
        <p><strong>Duke Sucellus — melee:</strong> collect the arena mushrooms/salt, grind and ferment the two poisons while dodging the extremities' gaze, then wake Duke. Use the slash/crush melee kit with Protect from Melee; stay near the pillar-safe side, move when a gas vent activates, and avoid the ice-spike slam. <strong>Whisperer — Magic:</strong> bring the blackstone fragment and affordable Magic-accuracy gear. The current Whisperer has a <strong>60% Earth weakness</strong>. Our reproducible damage plan is <strong>Earth Wave on the standard spellbook</strong> at the already-guaranteed 75 Magic, autocast with the purchased Ancient staff (or another owned compatible staff): each cast needs <strong>5 air, 7 earth and 1 blood rune</strong>, so budget a trial batch from the live bank. Earth Wave's 20 base max at 75 becomes a stronger ordinary hit against that weakness without any trident. Keep distance after her binding special rather than expecting a freeze. If you prefer <strong>Ancient ice spells</strong> to freeze that approach, switch to Ancients and use the same staff, accepting a slower damage lane; upgraded Iban's staff/Iban Blast is another <em>standard-book</em> fallback but does not exploit Earth weakness. Never describe Iban's spell or Earth Wave as usable while on Ancients. Pray against the incoming <strong>Magic or Ranged</strong> volleys, move after each set to avoid tentacles, activate the fragment for Shadow-Realm specials, kill a matching set of souls, step on the safe seeds and hide behind pillars for screeches. Protect sanity: the enraged ending is faster and still needs movement/prayer reads. This is a demanding mechanics fight even with the quest-version HP; do not sell the baseline as a guaranteed first try. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Whisperer" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Earth weakness and fight reference</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Final sequence:</strong> the Mysterious Figure switches protection prayers, so bring both melee and range and dodge the post-stun purple orb. Re-bank before the four wights; the deterministic slash/crossbow pair works, but that encounter restarts from the first wight if you leave or die. Watch the Assassin's poison clouds and use the white smoke, kill Ketla clones, and follow each later wight's movement/prayer mechanic rather than trying to tank the whole room. <strong>Deaths are not free/safe:</strong> quest boss graves can be outside the arena or at the relevant re-entry point; confirm the current in-game gravestone/reclaim prompt before each retry, retrieve promptly, and budget supplies. Wilderness-like zero-risk assumptions from Fight Caves do not apply. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Desert_Treasure_II_-_The_Fallen_Empire" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full quest boss mechanics and routes</a>.</p>
        <p>After completion, claim <strong>three ancient lamps of 100,000 XP each</strong>. Eligible skills at actual 60+ are <strong>Attack, Strength, Defence, Hitpoints, Ranged, Magic and Prayer</strong>—not Slayer. Read the live combat tab. <strong>Strength is the default</strong> if it has useful room to grow; Prayer or Hitpoints may have a clearer immediate payoff, or Strength may already be far ahead. This is three distinct lamps, allocated once each, not a new required combat target. Record the <strong>Ring of shadows</strong> and <strong>Scar essence mine</strong> unlocks. Post-quest boss uniques are entirely optional.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">3.5 complete · guaranteed route exit</div>
        <h3>The old Grandmasters and their prerequisite chains are closed.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quests:</strong> the named cleanup quests, Contact!, Beneath Cursed Sands, Enakhra's Lament, Secrets of the North, Dragon Slayer II and Desert Treasure II complete; Curse of the Empty Lord, The General's Shadow and His Faithful Servants complete as required miniquests.</li>
          <li><strong>Skills/rewards:</strong> actual 60+ Runecraft; DS2's fixed 80k Smithing/60k Mining/50k Agility/50k Thieving claimed; Contact's one two-use combat lamp, Ellen's four 25k choices and DT2's three 100k lamps each recorded once.</li>
          <li><strong>Carry forward:</strong> Fire Cape, actual 75+ Magic/Ranged and 74+ Slayer, deterministic crossbow/melee kit, live remaining bolt/rune/cash stock, Ring of shadows and Scar essence access. Read the <em>live</em> skill tab for the final Blood Moon Rises gaps; do not assume optional XP landed.</li>
